From: nabu port
Subject: [PATCH 0013] nabu: start processors with processor_boot (XNU 12377)

The full macOS 27.3 kernelcache under QEMU (series 0001-0012) stopped in
NabuCPU::startAll: "NABU CPU: processor_start cpu=0 failed: 5". In 12377,
processor_start() is processor_start_from_kext(), a no-op that returns
KERN_FAILURE. Registered processors are started with processor_boot(), boot
CPU first, then the others, as iokit/Kernel/arm/AppleARMSMP.cpp does; the
existing per-CPU wait on nabuStarted (set by initCPU) is kept.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/NabuCPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/NabuCPU.cpp
index 76ed7b2..5126adc 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/NabuCPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/NabuCPU.cpp
@@ -145,10 +145,13 @@ NabuCPU::startAll(void *arg __unused, wait_result_t result __unused)
 		if (cpu == NULL) {
 			panic("NABU CPU: missing nub for logical CPU %u", cpu_id);
 		}
-		kern_return_t kr = processor_start(cpu->machProcessor);
-		if (kr != KERN_SUCCESS) {
-			panic("NABU CPU: processor_start cpu=%u failed: %d", cpu_id, kr);
-		}
+		/*
+		 * XNU 12377: processor_start() is a kext no-op returning
+		 * KERN_FAILURE; processor_boot() starts a registered processor (boot
+		 * CPU first), as AppleARMSMP does. For a secondary it reaches
+		 * NabuCPU::startCPU (PSCI CPU_ON) through cpu_start().
+		 */
+		processor_boot(cpu->machProcessor);
 		nanoseconds_to_deadline(5 * NSEC_PER_SEC, &deadline);
 		while (__atomic_load_n(&cpu->nabuStarted, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE) == 0 ||
 		    !nabu_cpu_signal_is_enabled(cpu_id)) {
